<h1>Reading Aloud Helps, Study Finds</h1>
<p class=3D"byline">By Jane Reporter</p>
<p>Researchers announced today that reading aloud improves comprehension fo=
r many listeners.</p><p>The study followed two hundred participants over si=
x months and measured recall after each session.</p><figure><img src=3D"htt=
ps://news.example.com/chart.png" alt=3D"A chart of recall scores" width=3D"=
160" height=3D"100"></figure><p>Participants who listened while following t=
he text remembered noticeably more than those who only read silently.</p><p=
><img src=3D"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAA=
AAABAAEAAAIBRAA7" width=3D"1" height=3D"1" alt=3D""><p>The authors caution =
that the effect varied widely between individuals and between kinds of mate=
rial.</p>
